# === CELL 1: Imports, Constants & JobLauncher ===
__AGENT_VERSION__ = "3.6.7"  # alias=agent-version-global. v3.6.7 Fix#1 domain/product COMPLETENESS (healthcare base-MVM 59.5% RCA): vibe-TEXT named domains (workforce, reference) + products were dropped when the business_domains widget was EMPTY because only widget domains were pinned. (a) alias=vibe-named-entities-harvest: harvest scope=='domain'/'table' scope_targets from VibeOrchestrator.manifest -> _USER_PINNED_DOMAINS_RUNTIME + widgets _required_domains_from_vibe / _required_products_from_vibe + RAISE (never lower) the min/max_domains sizing floor so cap-tune cannot trim a named domain. (b) alias=vibe-named-domain-inject: P0.52 judge-inject now sources widget+vibe UNION (EXHAUSTIVE trim stays WIDGET-only since vibe-text names are an open minimum set per CLAUDE.md 3a-bis) and protects vibe-named domains from architect removal. (c) alias=vibe-named-product-musthave: vibe-named products merged into the architect must_have_set (reuses existing enforcement). (d) alias=vibe-completeness-gate: last-resort pre-physical re-inject of any required domain dropped after generation + LOUD log of still-missing required products for the agentic loop. PRIOR v3.6.6 SIX root-cause fixes from the healthcare base-MVM + ncdot v3.6.5 audit (CLAUDE.md 1a no-roadmap, fix all now). (1) alias=settags-sparkconnect-concurrency-cap + (2) alias=settags-transient-backoff: healthcare base-MVM SET TAGS failed 18292/18731 (97.65%) with [RequestId=...] server errors. PROVEN by warehouse-REST repro (1800 column tags @ 60 workers = 0.0% fail) that the loss is NOT UC metadata throttling but serverless Spark-Connect SESSION SATURATION: column-tag DDL runs via execute_sql->spark.sql() on the shared Connect session and ~20-way concurrent ALTER COLUMN SET TAGS trips a server-side concurrent-DDL limit that the weak 3x0.5s retry cannot recover -> cascading 97.7% loss. Fix caps the Spark-Connect DDL fan-out to a session-safe ceiling (default 8, config TAG_DDL_MAX_WORKERS) so the limit is never tripped, AND gives transient server errors real exponential backoff+jitter (>=5 attempts) while failing fast on permanent errors (COLUMN_NOT_FOUND/PARSE/42xxx). Serverless-safe (§2), industry-agnostic. (3) alias=selffixer-parse-structured-return: SelfFixer _call_opus assumed a JSON string but _v207_call_llm_spark_free/_call_ai_query can return an ALREADY-PARSED dict/list (response_schema structured output) -> json.loads(list) TypeError caught, then re.search on the list raised UNCAUGHT 'expected string ... got list' -> opus_call_failed on EVERY VREQ (healthcare SelfFixer fixed 0/N). Fix returns dict directly / first dict in a list, only runs json.loads+regex when raw is genuinely a string. (4) alias=sa-findings-into-selffixer-loop (user directive 'WHY YOU DID NOT INCLUDE THE STATIC ANALYSIS IN THE AGENTIC LOOP'): SA findings were surfaced ONLY to next_vibes.txt, never into _unfulfilled_for_next_vibe, so the SelfFixer closed loop NEVER attempted the structural residuals (denormalized_natural_key/cross_domain_duplicate/unlinked_fk) the deterministic autofix left behind. New _v366_sa_findings_requeue recomputes SA fresh on the shipped flat lists and queues each SelfFixer-fixable STRUCTURAL finding as a synthetic unfulfilled REQ (reuses the closed loop + run_metamodel_static_analysis, DRY). (5) alias=joblaunch-parent-force-exit: the parent launcher (launch-gate mode) did a BARE return after the child TERMINATED SUCCESS, never calling dbutils.notebook.exit(), so it hung ~41-60min on lingering non-daemon threads (ncdot run 23674965251537 + the v3.6.5 re-run both overhung). The v3.6.5 joblaunch-getrun-watchdog only capped the get_run poll stall, NOT this post-return hang. Fix routes the success path through _safe_notebook_exit (DRY) which submits the result, calls dbutils.notebook.exit() and arms the os._exit(0) teardown watchdog. (6) alias=ddl-failure-reason-summary + alias=settags-failure-category: SET TAGS failures were silent (worker-thread p_logger.error never reached the volume handler) or logged only the first 10 raw failures with err truncated at 100 chars (cut off the [ERROR_CODE] after the [RequestId=...] prefix); now aggregate a per-category failure histogram on the MAIN thread (guaranteed flushed) and widen err capture to 400 chars so RCA is possible from logs alone (§11). PRIOR v3.6.5: v3.6.5 alias=selffixer-route-aiquery-on-unresolved-endpoint: SelfFixer (closed-loop residual VREQ repair) was INERT on fe-gcp -- [selffixer-endpoint-resolve MISS] left self.llm_endpoint=None yet _call_opus still PREFERRED _v207_call_llm_spark_free(model=None) -> HTTP POST /serving-endpoints/None/invocations -> NotFound on every failed VREQ -> ncdot base-MVM run 748921978115629 shipped 60.87% verified adherence (DEAD AGENTIC REPAIR, exactly the failure class CLAUDE.md MISSION warns about). Root cause: _call_opus gated the spark-free HTTP path on hasattr(_v207) ALONE, ignoring whether a serving-endpoint name actually resolved; the proven main path _call_ai_query (which built the ENTIRE model on the SAME workspace, self-resolving the model via _get_model_config_for_prompt -> default databricks-claude-sonnet-4-5) was only the elif fallback never reached because hasattr(_v207) is always True on the real AIAgent. Fix gates the _v207 branch on (self.llm_endpoint AND hasattr) so an UNRESOLVED endpoint falls through to _call_ai_query instead of POSTing to a literal 'None' endpoint; behaviour UNCHANGED when an endpoint did resolve (llm_endpoint truthy still prefers the HTTP spark-free path). Generic/industry-agnostic, reuse-first (no new LLM path). v3.6.5 alias=joblaunch-getrun-watchdog: the parent launcher (Job Launch Gate self-relaunches the agent as a child job, then JobLauncher.wait_for_run_terminal polls the child) hung ~41min AFTER the child TERMINATED SUCCESS (ncdot run 23674965251537 @ fe-gcp) because SDK jobs.get_run() has NO client-side timeout -> a stalled control-plane call blocks the poll loop forever and the loop's own timeout_seconds check (only evaluated AFTER get_run returns) never fires, so the parent never observes the child's terminal state. Fix wraps each get_run in the v3.6.2 _io_with_timeout watchdog (120s/call); a timed-out call raises into the existing except -> re-polled next iteration, so transient stalls recover and permanent ones are still capped by overall timeout_seconds. Applied to BOTH duplicate wait_for_run_terminal defs (the 2nd shadows the 1st -- DRY debt noted). Reuse-first. v3.6.4 alias=clash-ignore-underscore-meta: _early_clash_detection heuristic (_list_user_schemas) and _check_physical_deployment_clash treated ANY non-{_metamodel,_metrics,default,information_schema} schema as a business-database clash, so a leading-underscore META schema (e.g. _staging where the driver/user stages the model_vibes input file, or _tmp/_archive a real user may have) FALSELY tripped the PHYSICAL DEPLOYMENT CLASH guard and aborted new-base-model with a ValueError. Business domain schemas are never underscore-prefixed (the agent own meta schemas _metamodel/_metrics already are), so both clash filters now also exclude every schema.startswith("_"). Generic/industry-agnostic. v3.6.3 alias=contextmanager-decorator-misplacement: v3.6.2 io-timeout-watchdog splice put @contextmanager on _io_with_timeout (plain tuple-returning fn) instead of _suppress_dbutils_stdout (yield generator used 14x via with) -> every `with _suppress_dbutils_stdout()` raised TypeError generator-not-CM and _io_with_timeout returned a _GeneratorContextManager not (val,timed_out); child new-base-model run crashed ~1.7min at step_setup_and_clean mkdirs (N1 INTERNAL_ERROR), driver merely polled the dead child (no real I/O hang). Fix moves @contextmanager onto _suppress_dbutils_stdout, removes from _io_with_timeout. v3.6.1 alias=unified-agentic-convergence: single exit policy (_agentic_loop_should_stop) shared by base-model architect (domain+global), resize (shrink/enlarge) and VOV apply loops, per user directive: the agentic loop runs for ANY operation and exits ONLY on good-quality, approaching-15h, or no-convergence; fixed iteration caps demoted to high safety ceilings (arch 3->8, vov 10->25, vov budget 300m->840m). PRIOR v3.6.0: v3.6.0 TWO root-cause fixes from the cross-industry v2 VOV audit (11 industries) that ran AFTER the v3.5.9 monotonic-guard landed. (FIX1 alias=monotonic-guard-sacount-severity) _sa_issue_count returned a SCALAR error+warning total, so the monotonic guard accepted a pass that traded many warnings for a NEW hard ERROR: semiconductors v2 dropped warnings 623->212 but introduced errors 0->1, total 623->213 looked 'better' and the regressed pass SHIPPED a hard error. An error is categorically worse than a warning; _sa_issue_count now returns a LEXICOGRAPHIC (error,warning) tuple so Python tuple-compare makes (1,212)>(0,623) True and the guard REVERTS any error increase regardless of warning movement. (FIX2 alias=p074-shared-canonical-keep) the P0.74 cross-domain collision-rename kept idxs[0] as canonical owner and QUALIFIED the rest into '<domain>_<name>'; when the colliding set included the 'shared'/'common' SSOT domain and it was not first, it became 'shared.shared_<x>' which the SA shared_domain_prefix rule flags as an ERROR — the rename and the rule were in direct conflict. Now a shared/common occurrence is always KEPT canonical (unqualified, the natural SSOT owner) and the non-shared colliders are qualified instead; falls back to first-sorted-domain when no shared owner is present (preserving the original v0.6.5 deterministic owner pick). Both deterministic, industry-agnostic. ALSO (test-infra, non-runtime) conftest.py worker-scoped agent_source cache + atomic write to kill a pytest-xdist write-race that flaked ~4 agent_helpers tests under -n. PRIOR: was 3.5.9. v3.5.9 FIVE root-cause fixes from the restaurants v2 VOV audit (user found 500 SA warnings + degraded model in next_vibes.txt while prior report claimed 100%): (FIX-A alias=vov-run-autofix-default + alias=autofix-monotonic-guard) the v2.0.8 'vov-review-finalize-skip-autofix' DELIBERATELY SKIPPED the entire pre-SA autofix on the VOV path at 3 sites (post-architect, post-QA, finalize), so denormalized_natural_key/cross_domain_duplicate/self_referencing_fk defects were NEVER cleaned and the model degraded version-over-version (restaurants v2 shipped 500 warnings, deterministic score floored at 50); now the autofix runs by default on VOV (opt-out only via SKIP_POST_VOV_AUTOFIX) wrapped in a monotonic guard that snapshots+reverts if SA ever gets strictly worse (the autofix is NOT idempotent: a 2nd raw pass exploded multi_fk_missing_label 18->152), GUARANTEEING the model never regresses (empirically 500->32 warnings on restaurants v2). (FIX-E alias=next-vibes-fresh-sa) step_generate_next_vibes trusted a stale pre-computed _static_analysis_result captured at post_finalize BEFORE later subdomain/metric-view/sample steps mutate the model, so next_vibes.txt reported issues that did not match the shipped model.json (the 'scoreboard lies'); now ALWAYS recomputes SA fresh on the final flat lists. (FIX-B alias=unlinked-fk-deterministic-relink) deterministically links any unlinked _id column whose name equals an existing product PK (unique target -> link; multiple -> prefer same-domain; cyclic -> defer to LLM/next_vibes via _would_create_cycle guard, NEVER trade an unlinked_fk for an R8 fk_cycle). (FIX self-ref alias=self-ref-preserve-correct-target) P0.24 was STRIPPING labeled self-referencing FKs whose column used a shorter stem than the PK (comparative_prior_period_id vs financial_period_id) turning them into unlinked_fk; now repoints them to the product PK. (FIX p074 alias=p074-pk-attr-sync) P0.74 qualify-rename set product.primary_key to the qualified form but left the PK attribute under the old name -> pk_attribute_missing error; now reconciles the PK attribute + repoints FKs. (FIX ssot alias=ssot-distinct-stemkey) _v291 cross-domain distinct marker went stale after a P0.74 rename re-surfacing cross_domain_duplicate; now also keyed by (stem, {domains}) so it survives the rename. PRIOR: was 3.5.8. v3.5.8 alias=v358-product-ceiling: ROOT CAUSE of the media_broadcasting/ngo VOV product EXPLOSION that v3.5.6's sizing-contradiction sanitizer did NOT stop — the merged sizing directive correctly carried max_total_products=421 (max==min, NO contradiction) yet VOV review-mode batch expansion added LLM-hallucinated products UNBOUNDED to 5214 because the cumulative product ceiling was enforced ONLY on the from-scratch base-ECM target_fit clamp (line ~89760), NEVER on the VOV path. Fix: a DETERMINISTIC finalize gate _v358_enforce_product_ceiling_flat wired in step_create_logical_schema at the canonical write-point (4-space top-level, runs for VOV; VOV-gated on the _v357 v1 snapshot so the base path keeps its own clamp) prunes the excess back to max_total_products while PROTECTING every v1 product (§3b USER source) + every vibe-mandated new entity (_vov_user_new_entities), dropping the LEAST-connected un-protected excess first (fewest FK in+out via attributes_data degree, then latest-added); NEVER drops a protected product (model floors at v1 count if v1>=ceiling). Generic/industry-agnostic; fires ONLY when total>ceiling so clean/bounded VOV runs are untouched. PRIOR: was 3.5.7. v3.5.7 THREE root-cause fixes from the v2-marathon GROUND-TRUTH VReq audit (CLAUDE.md 1a no-roadmap, fix all now). (RC1) alias=v357-move-bare-domain-target: _v337_extract_move_target only matched 'to X domain'/'to domain X' but the real vibe phrasing is 'move to <domain>' with NO 'domain' keyword ('move to product because...'), so EVERY move_product batch (21/22 ground-truth misses) deferred to the flaky LLM sandbox which raised 'mutator did not move any target product'; fix adds a bare-token-after-to/into pattern (apply step validates the token against real model domains, so a stopword/false token is safe -> defers). (RC2) alias=v357-preservation-gate: VOV dropped v1 products when rename/move batches conflicted and overwrote each other (13 product drops in the audit); a deterministic flat finalize gate restores any unaccounted v1 product (+its attributes) into its original or the most-populated surviving domain per §3b (tolerant of prefix-renames + applied_renames; skippable via _v357_skip_preservation). (RC3) alias=v357-junk-domain-validator: VOV/LLM mutation leaked sentinel words ('partially' automotive, 'unknown' consumer_goods) as DOMAIN names that survived to the final model; a finalize validator drops every junk/stopword-named domain and reassigns its products to the most-populated valid sibling (no real industry term is in the stoplist). All deterministic, industry-agnostic, wired at the live dispatch + flat finalize paths. PRIOR: was 3.5.5. v3.5.6 TWO root-cause fixes from the media_broadcasting/ngo VOV product-explosion audit (CLAUDE.md 1a no-roadmap, fix both now). (1) alias=v356-sizing-contradiction-sanitizer: the LLM VIBE_PARSE hallucinated tiny max_* values (max_domains=3/max_total_products=18/max_products_per_domain=6 -- the qualitative-smallness constants) from template PROSE ('It has THREE sections','Section 3') and the LLM+regex merge combined them with the regex-extracted EXPLICIT floor (min_domains=17/min_total_products=421), yielding a CONTRADICTORY directive (max_total_products=18 < min_total_products=421); the downstream ceiling logic discards a max<min contradiction -> NO product ceiling -> unbounded VOV expansion (media_broadcasting 421->4465 products / 50-100 quality, ngo 302->835). The v0.7.6 source-scale-guard was inert (business_context_raw empty at merge time). Fix: a DETERMINISTIC, source-INDEPENDENT sanitizer in the sizing merge lifts any max_* that is < its min_* floor up to the floor (explicit floor outranks a contradicting hallucinated max; matches clean-industry behaviour max==min==N); also widens max_products_per_domain when too small to hold the product floor across the domain floor. Fires ONLY on max<min so 'exactly N'/tiny-test vibes (max>=min) are untouched. Generic/industry-agnostic. (2) alias=v356-source-trace-parse-tags-coerce: _enforce_source_trace_tags._parse_tags did (s or '').split(',') on product/attr `tags` that VOV/sandbox mutations emit as list/dict -> AttributeError 'list' object has no attribute 'split' (media_broadcasting [source-trace-enforce ERROR] + B0040 rejected_unsafe mutator); fix reuses _coerce_tags_to_string_v250 (DRY) at the parse boundary, mirroring the v250/v355 enforcers. v3.5.5 alias=v355-enforce-string-product-fields-invariant: VOV/SelfFixer/sandbox mutations emit product-level string fields (source_domains/subdomain/data_type/association_edges/tags) as list/dict, so physical-build + table-tag + readme consumers calling .strip()/.lower()/.split() crashed 'list' object has no attribute 'strip' (v3.5.4 healthcare + media_broadcasting both died at ~13h in step_create_physical_schema_stage1 table-tag emit on product.source_domains, AFTER step 8d metric views had succeeded). Root cause: only ATTRIBUTE tags had a boundary string-coercer (v250); product-level string fields had none. Fix: new module-level _enforce_string_product_fields_invariant_v355 reuses _coerce_tags_to_string_v250 (DRY per 3d) and is called at all 3 consumer boundaries (step_create_physical_schema_stage1 after JSON sync, step_generate_readme, main install re-tag). Generic/industry-agnostic. v3.5.4 alias=nested-version-layout: on-volume artifact layout changed from fused '<scope>_v<n>' (ecm_v1) to nested 'v<n>/<scope>' (v1/ecm) to match data-models/<industry>/v<n>/{ecm,mvm}/ repo format; overview readme now lands at v<n>/readme.md and a new per-industry README.md landing (alias=industry-readme-landing) is written one level above v<n>/. No backward-compat read of old fused layout (industries rebuild from v1). Prior: v350 adds subdomain-name-enforce (S1): NCDOT vibe enumerated an EXPLICIT 9-name HR subdomain roster ('Employee Records','Recruitment & Onboarding',...) but the generator INVENTED its own subdomain labels (compensation_benefits, talent_acquisition, ...), none matching -> §3c USER-KING violation on every 'subdomain named X' VREQ. Fix: in _enforce_source_trace_tags, gated on the vibe enumerating a subdomain roster, ONE residual LLM per domain maps each product to the closest VIBE-DECLARED subdomain name (empty => keep current, so OPEN rosters healthcare/automotive are untouched) and we relabel product.subdomain (model.json authoritative via _enrich_model_authoritative_tags). Relabel-ONLY (subdomains are organisational labels, never FK targets) so it cannot orphan a column or break a join; idempotent. Generic/industry-agnostic. v349 adds subdomain-steward-enforce: the vibe names a 'Proposed Steward' per subdomain but product.steward/subdomain.steward were built EMPTY (the LLM only leaked some names into a product description), so the audit's S2 'stewards' VREQ scored 2/4 (partial) under the CORRECTED adherence formula (verified_applied / TOTAL_TRUE_VREQs, where extraction-misses count 0). Fix: in _enforce_source_trace_tags, when the vibe declares stewards, ONE residual LLM maps each distinct subdomain->steward (empty for N/A) and sets product.steward (model.json authoritative via _enrich_model_authoritative_tags) + a {prefix}subdomain_steward table tag (physical UC). Generic/industry-agnostic. ALSO (runner/verify_protocol.py, non-runtime): the physical oracle denominator was len(rows) (only the directives it PARSED) -> hid extraction misses; now denominator = TOTAL TRUE VREQs (--total-vreqs ground-truth, else agent-extracted-from-artifact proxy) and reports extraction coverage separately. was 3.4.8 (carried below). v348 NCDOT reverse-engineer provenance add-missing PER-VREQ AUDIT FIXES: (a) subdomain-user-sizing-respect — VREQ-013 mandated 9 HR subdomains but _clamp_and_validate_model_params hard-clamped max_business_subdomains 9->4 to tier bounds [3,4] EVEN under user_sizing_override because the subdomain keys were absent from _SIZING_PARAM_KEYS (tier heuristic overrode user directive, §3c); fix adds min/max_business_subdomains + min_products_per_subdomain to the override-exempt set. (b) trace-tag-harvest + trace-tag-physical-mirror — VREQ-011 mandated attribute-level tag ncdot_source_attribute=<orig> but the LLM emitted it as DESCRIPTION prose (181 attrs) not the tags field (8); _enrich_model_authoritative_tags harvests it into tag_set (model.json authoritative) AND _mirror_trace_tags_into_tags_string (called in step_finalize_model_before_physical_schema, BEFORE physical step_apply_tags reads the flat tags string) promotes it into the physical tags string so it becomes a real UC tag (9->190). (c) model-json-authoritative-tags — model.json now carries structured tag_set at domain/subdomain/table/column + first-class subdomain objects w/ steward; legacy 'tags' string preserved (backward compatible). was 3.4.6 (carried below). v346 CLOSED-DOMAIN-SET ROOT-CAUSE FIX (alias domain-closed-no-shared): NCDOT vibe declared 'BUILD EXACTLY THESE 2 DOMAINS - NOTHING ELSE' (sizing_directives min_domains==max_domains==2, EXHAUSTIVE widget ['hr','project']) yet the pipeline injected a 3rd SYSTEM-MANAGED 'shared' domain via _ensure_shared_domain (BOTH callers ran unconditionally) -> live v345 run had 3 domains -> VREQ-005/006 ('nothing else') physically VIOLATED (§3b/§3c USER-KING). Fix: (1) step_create_logical_schema stamps config['USER_DOMAINS_EXHAUSTIVE'] from the closed-roster signal onto the shared config dict (config IS widgets_values['config']); (2) _ensure_shared_domain SUPPRESSES 'shared' creation when that flag is set (single DRY gate covering both callers); (3) the global semantic-dedup keeps 'shared' OUT of valid_domains_set when closed so an LLM-proposed shared merge falls back to a SOURCE user domain instead of birthing a 3rd domain. Generic/industry-agnostic: silent on OPEN rosters (healthcare/automotive still get 'shared' for SSOT). was 3.4.4. v345 SANDBOX CODE-GEN ROOT-CAUSE FIX (aliases mutator-json-literal-alias, vov-undefined-name-hint, vov-list-dict-shape-hint): HEALTH ecm_v2 VOV mutators (LLM-generated Python) failed with NameError name 'null'/'TARGET_SPECS' is not defined and AttributeError 'list' object has no attribute 'get' -> rejected_unsafe x3 -> VREQs (0019,0064,0066,0085,0275) DROPPED. Fix: (1) mutator-json-literal-alias defines null=None/true=True/false=False in SUBPROCESS_RUNNER_PREFIX (same precedent as _re/_cp) so JSON-literal code resolves; (2) vov-undefined-name-hint adds an 'is not defined' class to _v204_ast_class_hints telling the LLM only model/data + stdlib exist (no TARGET_SPECS/CONFIG globals — inline literals); (3) vov-list-dict-shape-hint adds 'object has no attribute get/append' classes teaching the exact list/dict model shape so .get/.append land on the right collection. Generic, industry-agnostic, extends the existing hint table (DRY). v345 ALSO adds gt-tag-prefix-compound-violation: NCDOT VREQ-005 (65.2%) the physical ground-truth tag-prefix audit classified a COMPOUND key 'confidential,pii_address,ncdot_business_glossary_term' as a single industry key then tested .startswith('ncdot_') on the WHOLE string (fails, starts with 'confidential') even though every non-universal token DOES carry the prefix; fix makes the violation check per-token (a key violates iff some token is BOTH non-universal AND missing the prefix), reusing _is_universal_token (DRY). v345 ALSO adds mv-column-prevalidate-prune: NCDOT VREQ-016 (88.9%) the physical MV pre-validator DROPPED the WHOLE metric view hr_vacancy_rate when ONE dimension referenced a missing column (hr.position.description) -> physical MV count 2 != user 'EXACTLY 3'; fix prunes only the offending dimension/measure block and KEEPS the view (All Records/Row Count fallback if a section empties), consistent with the logical ColCheck pruner (DRY). v345 ALSO adds mv15-none-resp-guard: live HEALTH ecm_v2 7/209 mv15_fk_semantic_gate batches crashed AttributeError 'NoneType' has no attribute 'get' because ai_agent._call_ai_query can RETURN None on a non-rate-limit empty response WITHOUT raising, bypassing the except-block resp-None guard; fix guards the post-call resp shape (skip batch if not dict). was 3.4.3. v344 VIBE-DECLARED-CONVENTIONS ROOT-CAUSE FIX (aliases vibe-conventions-extract, vibe-conventions-override, gt-tag-prefix-compound-split): the LLM vibe-parse had NO model_conventions field, so a vibe declaring 'Tag prefix: ncdot_' 3x was dropped; business-context-gen then hallucinated tag_prefix='cg_' and all 2766 business_glossary_term tags shipped as cg_business_glossary_term (not ncdot_business_glossary_term) -> NCDOT VREQ-004+VREQ-014 physically FAILED at 56.5%. Fix: (1) vibe-conventions-extract adds model_conventions to _VIBE_PARSE_RESPONSE_SCHEMA + VIBE_PARSE_PROMPT so the LLM extracts declared tag/schema prefix+suffix, naming, cataloging; (2) vibe-conventions-override makes _parse_with_llm OVERRIDE the setup-resolved config TAG_PREFIX/SCHEMA_*/MODEL_CONVENTIONS (built from LLM-generated cg_) with vibe-declared values per CLAUDE.md 3c (USER-KING); (3) gt-tag-prefix-compound-split splits comma-joined classification values (restricted,pii_dob) before the prefix check so universal tags are not false-flagged. Generic/industry-agnostic, no regex (honours v0.9.4 LLM-only). v332 VERIFIER METADATA-BLINDNESS FIX (aliases verifier-snapshot-metadata, verifier-relation-remove-column): the per-VREQ verifier snapshot exposed only products+attributes, omitting tags/metric_views/catalog -> LLM verifier false-failed every tag/MV/catalog VREQ (NCDOT mvm_v8: 785 tagged attrs + 6 MVs reported as absent), and remove_fk was verified at TABLE level so removing one column FK among many always failed. Fix surfaces untruncatable tag/MV/catalog inventories + column-level remove_fk verification (also lifts the L2 ground-truth audit which reuses _verify_deterministic). 16 of 18 confirmed false-fails on NCDOT eliminated; raises measured precision 39.7%->~63% on the same model. Generic/industry-agnostic.
# v0.9.5 legacy header preserved: # alias=agent-version-global v0.9.5 NEW FEATURE [vibe-lineage-artifact FIRED] - new vibes/vibe_lineage.json artifact written after every vibe-driven run (new base model, vibe modeling of version, shrink ecm, enlarge mvm). Maps each user vibe -> LLM interpretation -> the concrete model objects (domain/product/attribute/relationship/metric_view) added/removed/modified, with logical and physical FQNs + per-field before/after. Composes existing capture_vibe_model_snapshot + VibeManifest + write_to_dbfs (no new diff engine). Best-effort attribution via vibe_master_actions.mapped_req_ids then scope_targets prefix match; changes that cannot be tied to a requirement land in the _unattributed bucket with source=pipeline. Skipped for install/uninstall/generate-samples (no vibe parsing happens). aliases: vibe-lineage-artifact, vibe-lineage-snapshot, vibe-lineage-hydrate, vibe-lineage-diff, vibe-lineage-attribution, vibe-lineage-skip, vibe-lineage-reqs. // v0.9.4 LLM-ONLY VIBE EXTRACTION header preserved below for audit trail:
